 [case id=vc-016-valid-predicate-reachable level=core gate=enforced
  [tags vc valid lexicon issue-739]
  [meta [#
note: RULED 739-1a. This case used to pin a CXER0100 parse failure —
note: `[$vc:valid? …]` could not be written, because the lexicon does not
note: admit `?` inside an identifier, so the §3 predicate had no call form
note: at all. Renamed `valid` cutover-first; the pin now asserts the
note: surface WORKS rather than that it does not exist.
note:
note: An unsigned [vc] is not verifiable, so the predicate answers false —
note: which is the point: it ANSWERS. Reaching a `false` is the whole
note: difference from a parse error.
#]]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/vc']
[$vc:valid [vc id="urn:vc:1"] 2026-06-16T12:30:00Z]
#]]
  [out-text [#
false
#]]
 ]

